## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant masking, macro-driven schema generation, and lineage tracking in dbt, while enforcing isolation and late data.

## Key Concepts
- Macro-driven per-tenant schemas
- Policy-based PII masking (redact, hash, partial)
- Global lineage table and dependency tracking
- Late-arrival handling and tenant isolation CI

## Code Example

```sql
-- macro: mask_pii
{% macro mask_pii(policy, field) -%}
  {% if policy == 'redact' -%}
    NULL
  {% elif policy == 'hash' -%}
    SHA2(CONCAT(COALESCE('{{tenant_id}}', 'global'), {{field}}), 256)
  {% else -%}
    {{ field }}
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test masking across tenants with different policies?
- How would you extend lineage to support multi-tenant drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a safe, production-grade debugging workflow leveraging Time Travel and dbt macros while preserving tenant isolation and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped debug mirroring
- dbt macros for environment toggling
- Snowflake Time Travel for backfills
- CI gating and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro swap_tenant_debug(tenant, mode) -%}
  {% if mode == 'debug' -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_{{tenant}}.debug_hourly_engagement;
  {% else -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_base.hourly_engagement;
  {% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you safely expire old debug objects?
- How would you audit backfill changes across tenants?
